{"comment_text": {"ja58:0.1": "", "ja58:0.2": "", "ja58:0.3": "", "ja58:0.4": "", "ja58:1.1": "", "ja58:1.2": "", "ja58:1.3": "<i lang='pi' translate='no'>Dakkhiyaṁ</i> is an abstract neuter noun from <i lang='pi' translate='no'>dakkha</i> having the sense “adroitness”. It is formed by analogy with <i lang='pi' translate='no'>sūriyaṁ</i>, which here means “heroism”; compare <i lang='pi' translate='no'>vīriya</i> in the same sense. ", "ja58:1.4": "", "ja58:2.1": ""}, "html_text": {"ja58:0.1": "<article id='ja58'><header><ul><li class='division'>{}</li>", "ja58:0.2": "<li>{}</li>", "ja58:0.3": "<li>{}</li></ul>", "ja58:0.4": "<h1 class='sutta-title'>{}</h1></header>", "ja58:1.1": "<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja58:1.2": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja58:1.3": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja58:1.4": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span></p></blockquote>", "ja58:2.1": "<p class='endsutta'>{}</p></article>"}, "root_text": {"ja58:0.1": "Jātaka ", "ja58:0.2": "Ekakanipāta ", "ja58:0.3": "Āsīsavagga ", "ja58:0.4": "8. Tayodhammajātaka ", "ja58:1.1": "“Yassa ete tayo dhammā, ", "ja58:1.2": "vānarinda yathā tava; ", "ja58:1.3": "Dakkhiyaṁ sūriyaṁ paññā, ", "ja58:1.4": "diṭṭhaṁ so ativattatī”ti. ", "ja58:2.1": "Tayodhammajātakaṁ aṭṭhamaṁ. "}, "translation_text": {"ja58:0.1": "Stories of Past Lives 58 ", "ja58:0.2": "The Book of the Ones ", "ja58:0.3": "Hope ", "ja58:0.4": "Three Qualities: a past life story ", "ja58:1.1": "Whoever possesses these three qualities ", "ja58:1.2": "like you, lord of langurs—", "ja58:1.3": "adroitness, heroism, wisdom—", "ja58:1.4": "escapes the visible foe. ", "ja58:2.1": ""}, "variant_text": {"ja58:0.1": "", "ja58:0.2": "", "ja58:0.3": "", "ja58:0.4": "", "ja58:1.1": "Yassa ete → yassete (sya1ed, sya2ed, pts-vp-pli1, mr) ", "ja58:1.2": "", "ja58:1.3": "", "ja58:1.4": "", "ja58:2.1": ""}, "reference_text": {"ja58:0.1": "", "ja58:0.2": "", "ja58:0.3": "", "ja58:0.4": "", "ja58:1.1": "dr27.20, 